# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM fallback chain. All free tiers, no card required.
#
# Providers are tried in the order below and the chain stops at the first one
# that answers and passes the output guard. A provider needs BOTH a key and a
# model to take part, otherwise it is skipped. With none set the app still
# runs and serves canned verdicts.
#
# To take a provider out of rotation, blank its key. Do that rather than
# leaving a dead one first in the chain, since every request pays a failed
# round trip before moving on.
#
# RUN `npm run models` AFTER ADDING A KEY. It asks each provider what it
# actually serves and flags a pinned name that is no longer in the list. Names
# get retired constantly, and a stale one is a silent 404 that drops every
# request to canned verdicts with no visible error.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Groq — ~1k requests/day per model.  https://console.groq.com
GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# 2. Google Gemini — ~1,500 requests/day.  https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#    "-latest" is an alias that tracks the current Flash release, so a rename
#    upstream does not quietly break us.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest

# 3. Cerebras — ~1M tokens/day, fastest of the lot.  https://cloud.cerebras.ai
#    Returns 402 "payment required" once the free allowance is spent.
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
CEREBRAS_MODEL=gpt-oss-120b

# --- Optional extras. All OpenAI-compatible, so they need no code change. ---

# 4. OpenRouter — one key, many models.  https://openrouter.ai/keys
#    50 requests/day on an unfunded account, 1,000/day after a one-off $10.
#    "openrouter/free" auto-routes across whatever free models are up, which
#    is why it is the default here: it cannot go stale.
#    Browse the rest: https://openrouter.ai/models?max_price=0
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_MODEL=openrouter/free

# 5. NVIDIA NIM — large open-weight catalogue.  https://build.nvidia.com
#    Wants a phone number. No default model: run `npm run models nvidia`
#    and paste one, since their catalogue moves faster than this file.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
NVIDIA_MODEL=

# 6. GitHub Models — free with any GitHub account, no phone.
#    Make a token at https://github.com/settings/tokens with models:read.
#    Run `npm run models github` for the current list.
GITHUB_MODELS_TOKEN=
GITHUB_MODEL=

# 7. Mistral — free tier, wants a phone number.  https://console.mistral.ai
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_MODEL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rate limiting (optional)
#
# Without these, limits are counted per server instance in memory: fine
# locally, close to useless on serverless where requests spread across many
# instances. Add before putting the link anywhere public.
# https://console.upstash.com
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Salt for hashing client IPs. Raw IPs are never stored or logged. Only
# matters once Upstash is in use, since that is when the hashes persist.
# Generate one: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
RATELIMIT_SALT=
